  "notes": [
   "Only the two instruction pages were provided (no inventory pages), so Element IDs are not known. Part types are best-guess matches from the catalogue (colour in props); three new types were added for pieces with no obvious match.",
   "The model is two builds: the mailbox (steps 1-3 of the first column), the flower/bakery-style display stand (steps 1-8 of the other columns), plus Stephanie (hair, head, torso, skirt) holding a letter.",
   "Stand steps 1-4 are hard to read in the pictures: the white base (2x4 brick plus two 1x4 bricks), black grille, black 2x2 plate, white bottles with brown tops are inferred. A white plate on top of the bottles in step 4 was not modelled separately.",
   "The flower stem takes three pink flowers; all three are recorded on the stem's single stud port because the stem's exact stud layout is unclear. The red slope/board seen in step 5 is inferred.",
   "Step 7 sub-assembly (white 2x4 plate, red pin piece, two pink roof slopes, white 1x1 brick with hole) rests on the brown bottle tops; step 8 adds two red heart halves on the roof.",
   "The mailbox roof is shown in step 3 with no parts box; modelled as a pink 2x2 slope on the red body. Letter is held in Stephanie's hand (contact only)."
  ]
